arm is load-store architecture 

in THUMB...

load (LDR) from memory into a register
store (STR) from a register into memory

registers can hold data, adresses, or instructions

e.g.

LDR r4, r3

loads the contents of the address (memory) that is referenced by r3 into register r4.

---------------------------------------------------------------

STR r4, r5

stores the contents of r4 into the address which is referenced by r5.

 
